@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+---
+id: task-005-cancel-booking
+type: task
+title: "Cancel booking"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Cancel booking
+
+Plans change, and customers ask the desk to cancel their bookings. The rental service gets a `cancel` operation
+that cancels a booking at a given time and reports the amount refunded.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `cancel(bookingId, at)` on the rental service cancels the booking `bookingId` at the instant `at`, an ISO-8601
+  UTC string as the other times of the module.
+- It returns `{ bookingId, refund }`: `bookingId` is the id of the cancelled booking, and `refund` is the amount
+  given back to the customer, in integer euro cents.
+- Refund policy (task-001, rule 5): a booking cancelled less than 24 hours before its start gets no refund, so
+  `refund` is 0; otherwise the full amount paid, which is the booking's `total` (discounted if the booking was),
+  is refunded. Exactly 24 hours before the start is not less than 24 hours, so it is refunded in full. A
+  cancellation at or after the start is less than 24 hours before the start and gets no refund.
+- A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment: `book` and `availability` treat its period as free again.
+- A booking can only be cancelled once. Cancelling it again is rejected.
+- An unknown `bookingId` is rejected.
+- A malformed `at` is rejected, as other malformed times are.
+- `cancel` is part of the `RentalService` interface and its result type is exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- The README no longer says that cancellations are not implemented.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1: cancelling a booking at least 24 hours before its start returns its total as the refund.
+- AC2: cancelling exactly 24 hours before the start refunds the full total.
+- AC3: cancelling less than 24 hours before the start returns a refund of 0.
+- AC4: cancelling at or after the start returns a refund of 0.
+- AC5: a booking with the long-stay discount refunds its discounted total.
+- AC6: after a cancellation, `availability` lists the item again for the cancelled period.
+- AC7: after a cancellation, `book` accepts an overlapping period for the same item.
+- AC8: cancelling the same booking twice is rejected.
+- AC9: cancelling an unknown booking id is rejected.
+- AC10: a malformed `at` is rejected.
+- AC11: cancelling one booking does not free another booking of the same item.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Implements the cancellation policy of task-001 (rule 5) and the cancellation criteria left open there (its AC7
+"no cancellation API is exposed" is superseded for this change). Each acceptance criterion maps to one or more
+tests in `src/rental.test.ts`.
